Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Oct 4 08:20:02 2026 -0500

    feat(cron): reject near-cap solves; solver bounds contract for sim-style solutions (DF-OFF-BY-ONE-31)
    
    Closes the remaining gap from DF-OFF-BY-ONE-30: the per-solve memory cap
    kills a runaway solve, but a solve that survived the cap while paging near
    it could still be committed as a "pre-verified" answer. This change adds
    harness-side rejection plus the prompt-side bounds contract.
    
    Harness side (internal/cron/loop.go processOne): after the peak RSS is
    observed, a solve that returned success but peaked above the reject
    threshold is REJECTED — the queue entry is marked failed with a reason
    naming the problem class, the measured peak and the threshold (gibStr),
    the loop counts it as a failure plus a dedicated SolveRejected counter,
    and the observer record carries the new Rejected field. Nothing reaches
    the graph.
    
    The threshold is cron.Config.SolveRejectRSSBytes, wired from the new
    -solve-reject-rss-mb flag (env OFF_BY_ONE_SOLVE_REJECT_RSS_MB): default -1
    = auto (DefaultSolveRejectFraction, 80% of -solve-mem-mb via
    SolveRejectThreshold), 0 = disabled, >0 = explicit MiB. With no cap
    configured the derived form is disabled (nothing to approach).
    
    Solver side (scripts/pi-agent): the solve prompt now carries a resource
    bounds contract for simulation-style problems — declare explicit bounds
    (max simulated events/packets/seconds) and aggregate incrementally rather
    than retaining a record per event. This is the fix direction for the
    2026-10-03 47 GB incident (a generated packet simulator appending once per
    simulated event).
    
    Tests: loop rejection/acceptance/disabled cells driven by a scripted RSS
    sampler (measured peak present in the reason, zero commits on rejection),
    the threshold derivation + flag-default matrix, the observer roll-up, and
    a source assertion that the wrapper contract cannot silently regress.
    Docs: "Solve memory bounds" section in docs/api-reference.md.
    
    Co-Authored-By: totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
